content.text:
Responsive: @media max-width 980 garage-body becomes 1fr (existing rule). At mobile the 3-col will collapse; car preview hidden behind. Add `.garage-body` mobile remains list. Fine.

Need mobile menu: words. Later screenshots.

Now the big game.js. Let me write carefully.

```js
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { RoomEnvironment } from 'three/addons/environments/RoomEnvironment.js';
...
const START_Z = -1.42;
const LANE = 4.2;
const FINISH = 402.336;
const RIVAL_POWER = [...]
```

`simulateBestET(spec)` for target.

Game class fields:
- canvas, renderer, scene, camera, clock, mode='boot', cameraMode='cockpit'
- save, audio, ui, track, effects, player, rival
- input = {throttle:false, clutch:false, steer:0, steerTarget:0, brake:false}
- keys={}
- touch = {gas:false, clutch:false, steer:0}
- wheelPointer=null
- race state: phase='idle', raceClock, greenClock, treeTimes, ambersOn, foul, playerRunStart, etc.

Cars creation:
```js
const paint = PAINTS.find(p=>p.id===save.paints[save.selected])?.hex || '#ff5a12';
this.player = createCarModel({paint, interior:true});
this.playerGroup = new THREE.Group(); this.playerGroup.add(this.player.root); this.scene.add(...)
```
`player.root` includes shadow and body. Set position (LANE,0,START_Z). Rotation? car forward +Z, no rotation.

Rival model paint from RIVAL_PAINTS[index], interior false. Hide group initially.

Spec:
```js
this.playerSpec = buildSpec(carById(save.selected), save.upgrades[save.selected]);
this.playerSim = new DragSim(this.playerSpec);
```
Rebuild whenever car/upgrade changes (garage). For race reset.

Rival spec computed per race:
```js
this.rivalInfo = this.pickRival();
this.rivalSpec = buildSpec(carById(info.car), info.upgrades);
this.rivalSpec.torque *= info.power;
this.rivalSim = new DragSim(this.rivalSpec);
```
Rebuild rival model if car changed: simplest, rebuild the model on each race? Model creation cost is fine, but dispose old. Or create all 4 car models? Simpler: create rival model at startRace with the chosen car config, paint; remove old from scene, dispose geometries/materials (some shared). Since we can't easily dispose shared mats, just remove from scene and let GC (GPU resources leak per race). Better rebuild only when car/paint changes; keep a map. Over 8 races it's minor. I'll implement `rebuildRivalModel(info)` disposing old root traversal geometry+material only if not shared... Could just build a model for each of the 4 car types once and swap visibility! 4 rival models, each with a paint color from the rival's palette. That's 4 extra car meshes in memory, each ~60 meshes, 240 meshes, mostly hidden. Draw calls only for visible. Good. But paints differ per rival; use each rival's own model with its own paint. Build 8? No, only 4 types; the same type used by multiple rivals would share paint. Could set paint when showing, using per-model paint material (unique per model) → works. So build one model per car type for rivals, and set paint on show. 4 models. Great. Group visibility hidden.

But note `mats.taillight` shared across all car models, and setPaint changes paintMat unique. Fine.

Menu/garage: the player car model isn't rebuilt on upgrades (not needed). On car change, rebuild player model with interior. Simpler to rebuild player model each time selected car changes. Dispose old root: traverse dispose geometry only (materials shared except paint). Paint material dispose. Do:
```js
this.scene.remove(this.playerGroup);
this.playerGroup.traverse(o=>{ if(o.isMesh) o.geometry.dispose(); });
```
Shared geometries? Each car model creates its own geometries, so fine. Materials: shared constants should NOT be disposed. Only paintMat dispose. Skip material disposal to be safe.

Player model root inside playerGroup. Rebuild.

`applySelectedCar()` rebuilds spec + model. Called on select/buy/upgrade? Upgrades don't require model change. Rebuild sim spec.

Position: car group at lane.

Camera menu orbit needs car at start. Good.

Rival preview not shown in menu (hidden).

Race start rebuild rival sim and show chosen model. Player sim reset.

Race flow details:

```js
startRace() {
  if (this.mode === 'race' || this.mode === 'raceover') ... restart anyway
  this.audio.init(); this.audio.ui();
  this.mode = 'race';
  this.phase = 'staging';
  this.raceClock = 0;
  this.greenClock = null;
  this.treeStartDelay = 1.2 + Math.random()*0.7;
  this.amberTimes = [treeStartDelay, treeStartDelay+0.6, treeStartDelay+1.2];
  this.greenAt = treeStartDelay + 1.75;
  this.foul=false; this.playerLaunched=false; this.playerRunStart=null;
  this.playerFinished=false; this.rivalFinished=false; ...
  this.rivalInfo = this.pickRival();
  setup rival model/spec/sim
  reset player sim/spec; playerGroup pos ...
  this.rivalGroup pos ...
  this.cameraMode='cockpit'; this.camSnap = true;
  this.ui.showHUD(this.rivalInfo.name);
  this.track.setTree(...false);
  this.effects.clear();
  this.lastClutch = false;
  this.toast...
  this.ui.setPhase("PREPARE-SE");
  this.treeFlags = [false,false,false,false]; // beep flags
}
```

Careful: after results, mode='result', startRace again should work. `mode` not 'race'? Set mode='race'.

`pickRival()`:
```js
const idx = Math.min(save.careerWins, RIVALS.length-1);
const base = RIVALS[idx];
const extra = Math.max(0, save.careerWins - (RIVALS.length-1));
const power = RIVAL_POWER[idx] + extra*0.04;
const info = {...base, power};
info.target = rivalTargetET(info);
return info;
```

`rivalTargetET(info)`: need simulation. Implement:
```js
function simulateET(spec) {
  const sim = new DragSim(spec);
  const dt=1/120;
  // stage rev
  for (let i=0;i<200;i++){ sim.step(dt,{throttle: sim.engineRpm<spec.launchRpm?1:0.2, clutch:true}, true); if (sim.engineRpm>=spec.launchRpm) break; }
  for(let i=0;i<20;i++) sim.step(dt,{throttle:0.1,clutch:true},true);
  sim.justReleased ...
  let t=0;
  while (sim.distance < FINISH && t<20) { sim.step(dt,{throttle: sim.wheelspin>0.6?0.65:1, clutch:false}, false); sim.autoShift(); t+=dt; }
  return sim.time;
}
```
Return ET since start of run including staged time? We only measured after release. Use separate `elapsed` sum. Return t. Cache by key. Note gap: the rival target ET from data ~; good.

Wait, the rival sim in the race uses reaction delay and no modulated throttle (we could modulate during wheelspin like the test). Let's implement AI throttle = 0.65 when wheelspin > 0.6 to avoid excessive spin — this makes the AI perform like the target simulation. Use same logic in both. Good.

`this.rivalReaction = 0.16 + Math.random()*0.14 + (1 - idx/8)*0.06`.

Update loop:
```
update(dt) {
  this.time += dt;
  if (this.mode==='race') {
    this.raceClock += dt;
    this.updateTree();
    this.updateRace(dt);
  } else if (menu/garage) { idle sim updates? }
  updatePlayerVisual(dt)
  updateRivalVisual(dt)
  updateCamera(dt)
  effects.update(dt)
  updateHUD()
